  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1012 PM MDT Wed Oct 28 2026\n\nSouthwest flow aloft is increasing as upper low nears the California \ncoast...and several short waves out ahead of the low near Baja\nrotate east toward New Mexico. This flow will bring up existing \nsub-tropical moisture over northern Mexico, including some \nmoisture from TS Vance, across the CWA Thursday. PWs approach one\ninch from the RG Valley east. Batted around a flood watch but \ndecided not to issue one. The moisture, decent instability and \nslow storm movement could still create a few flooding storms. \n\nOne of the short waves rotating out of the California trough reaches \nNew Mexico late FRIDAY afternoon and into the evening to spread \nanother round of showers/storms to the area. PWs almost as high as \nThursday's event, with sub-tropical jet approaching and drawing in \nmoisture from the eastern Pacific. Shear environment looks better \nthan Thursday, and along with modest CAPE values may be more \nconducive to some strong/severe storms. The negative is that the \nstorms are not likely to start until late in the day. \n\nSATURDAY (Halloween) looks to be a tweener day as the short wave \nexits the area and we await the the west coast upper low. Both \nGFS/ECMWF dampen the low as it approaches, but phasing it in with \nthe Pac NW over the Great Basin SUNDAY. This looks to be a fast \nmoving feature, though ECMWF somewhat slower. GFS moves it out by \nlate Sunday night while the ECMWF lets it hang around until Monday \nafternoon. Showers/storms should start out west Sunday afternoon and \nspread east through the evening hours. Once again PWs approach or \nslightly exceed one inch, suggesting some flood potential. \nHowever mid-level storm motion winds of 30-50 mph may not allow \nfor prolonged rain over any specific area. \n\nMain Pacific cold front moves through late Sunday night with \nsecondary colder front dropping out of the Great Basin to the CWA \nMonday night. High temps by Tuesday may remain in the 60s across the \nlowlands.",
